Perform Backup of Server via VCenter

Cut a Change task to the Wintel team to take snapshot of the nodes to be upgraded


 

Verify that the .NET 4.8 Framework Installed
The .NET 4.8 Framework must be installed on each CCP Server.
Navigate to the Registry and look for the Version number as shown in this illustration
 


Upgrade Central Credential Provider (CCP)

For UAT
	• Pre-Requisite
		○ Ensure the VIP NonPROD CCP address is working: 
 https:// ccpcert-test.cna.com/AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)-- With Certificate
https:// ccp-test.cna.com /AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)--Without Certificate


○ Ensure the CCP is working at the web server address:  
https://vskau1p1216.cna.com/AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)
https://vskau1p1217.cna.com/AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)
https://vskch1d921.cna.com/AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)
https://vskch1d922.cna.com/AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)








For Prod

https:// www.ccpcert.cna.com/AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)--With Certificate
https:// www.ccp.cna.com/AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)--Without Certificate


○ Ensure the CCP is working at the web server address:  
https:// vskau1p1231.cna.com/AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)
https:// vskau1p1232.cna.com//AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)
https:// vskblyd0004.cna.com/AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)
https:// vskblyd0005.cna.com /AIMWebService/V1.1/AIM.asmx (Expect AIMWebService page)


 

Ensure .NET Framework 4.8 is installed
	Check/Confirm:  
The version of .NET Framework (4.5 and later) installed on a machine is listed in the registry at HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\NET Framework Setup\NDP\v4\Full.  If the Full subkey is missing, then .NET Framework 4.5 or above isn't installed.
			§ If not, download offline installer here:  Microsoft .NET Framework 4.8 offline installer for Windows - Microsoft Support







Remove CCP Node from VIP by setting Offline

	Launch Schedule task and set component Offline

 



	Navigate to C:\log\Set_Component_Status.logs and check status of script 
 

		
	• Phase 1
	Create a backup of the C:\inetpub\wwwroot folder in entirety backup on C: Temp\(Pre-Upgrade 14.XXX)

	Create a backup of the  E:\Program Files\CyberArk\ApplicationPasswordProvider and move to C: Temp\(Pre-Upgrade 14.XXX)

	Take a snapshot of the AIMWEBSERVICE SSl and Authentication settings

 


 

	• Phase 2

		○ Uninstall the CCP web service:
			§ From the list of programs in Windows, uninstall the CCP web service, CyberArk AIMWebService.

 


NOTE:  If you defined multiple security configurations and authentication methods for the CCP web service, you must delete the respective virtual applications from the IIS Manager. See Multiple security configurations and authentication methods for the Central Credential Provider web service.

		○ Install the CCP Web Service by using the 'setup' application in the installer directory
		○ In the Welcome, click Next
		○ In the Select Installation Address, click Next
		○ In the confirm Installations, click Next
		○ In the Installation Complete, click Close


For Silent install

Copy the content from the installation package's \Central Credential Provider\Central Credential Provider Web Service folder into the local \Central Credential Provider\Central Credential Provider Web Service folder that you created above.

Run the below

 msiexec.exe  /i "<CCP Install Path>\AIMWebService.msi" /qn


Enable Hash
○ To enable hash authentication of the web service, calculate and configure the hash using the NetAIMGetAPPInfo utility.

	Go to C:\Program Files\CyberArk\ApplicationPasswordProvider\Utils folder, rename the NetPasswordSDK.dll to NetPasswordSDK.dll.NEW

	Copy the NetAIMGettAPPInfo.exe and the NetPAsswordSDK.dll file from the ApplicationPasswordProvider folder in Backup folder C: Temp\(Pre-Upgrade 14.XXX).

	Paste into the C:\Program Files\CyberArk\ApplicationPasswordProvider\Utils folder

	Open Powershell as administrator from C:\Program Files\CyberArk\ApplicationPasswordProvider\Utils folder and run the following:

	.\NETAIMGetAppInfo.exe GetHash  /AppExecutablesPattern="C:\inetpub\wwwroot\AIMWebService\bin\AIMWebService.dll"


		 
		Save old Hash Until all environments are running
		9F831EDD8180FE2869E87B38C3A8786F1E96129B8FC928A4A20CA104BCAB7DFF7924D52844412DD1A1AA3D7ECF71630445E6638EA005E7EE533788B3E9510BD0
		
	Add the new hash to the AimWebService AppID from PVWA interface, delete old.
		
	Compare the web.config in the installation directory, to the web.config which you backed up prior to upgrade.  

	Make any changes/updates if necessary (requires to move the Web.config file to Desktop, Edit, then move back)
		

			
		
	• Phase 3

	 Test the CCP installation using the CCP scripts for the various endpoints. 
	*NOTE: CCP Tests for Certificate auth, The client cert must be in user personal store, not computer
		○ Reset the NetPasswordSDK.dll back to the new one.

